WEBVTT

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.270
<i>Surfing all the time...</i>

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.490
<i>and, of course, working pretty 
hard in my schoolwork, too,</i>

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.800
<i>I managed to make it safely through 
my first year of high school.</i>

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.500
<i>Over the spring break that would send me 
into my second year of high school,</i>

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.740
<i>I went home for the first time in a year.</i>

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.760
<i>Which means it had also been a year 
since I'd last been in the ocean in Oarai.</i>

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.260
The waves here...

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.930
They really are the best!

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:48.020
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:54.200
Wave 12

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.450
What do you think, Kosuke-san?

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.000
Oarai's waves are the best, right?

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.200
They're not bad.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.030
But they can't beat Shonan's!

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.440
You just can't be honest, can you?

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.800
According to my analysis,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.290
both Oarai and Shonan have 
a surfer satisfaction rate of 92%.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:14.370
Which means that both are "the best."

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:19.800
<i>When I went back home, I invited Kosuke-san 
and Yuta to come train with me.</i>

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.120
<i>And Naoya, too.</i>

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.560
Naoya! What's wrong?

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.740
Kido seems kinda down.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.910
Has something happened 
with the Miruru anime again?

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.660
Hey, Naoya!

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.090
Naoya!

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.830
There's going to be a movie.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.080
Yeah. It's opening soon, right?

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.960
That's a good thing, isn't it?

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.390
You bought every kind 
of advance ticket you could find.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.080
You were super happy, right?

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.450
Not that...

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:52.590
There's going to be a Hollywood 
movie... a live-action one!

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.760
Hollywood?

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.040
So, she's spreading her wings and 
setting off into the world before us, huh?

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.340
That Miruru... Not bad!

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.570
Congratulations!

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.500
Oh!

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.340
A good wave! I'm taking it!

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.860
I'm not gonna let Miruru beat me. 
I'm heading out into the world, too!

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.860
Hey! Stop! I'm riding that wave!

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.660
The one heading out into the world 
is me, Iwana Kosuke!

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:17.610
And me!

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.580
Analysis complete!

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.210
Is that Hinaoka?

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.850
That's what I heard!

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.940
He's like a completely different person 
from when he left Oarai!

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.140
He's not getting outperformed 
by Iwana at all.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.960
He's pretty good!

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.150
There's a story going around 
that Fuke Rindo has acknowledged him.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.920
Wow... That's impressive.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:00.650
It's so cold.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.630
He's worried about the casting? 
So that's why he's down.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:10.190
And sometimes in a live-action work, 
everything ends up looking too different.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.610
If my Miruru... comes out looking
completely different, what will I do?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.100
No matter what kind of wave a wave is, 
they're all waves, right?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.290
Huh?

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:27.430
No matter what Miruru looks 
like, she's still Miruru!

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:32.250
Just like I am me! I'm no one else!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.140
Right?

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:37.350
What is it that Masaki is trying to say?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.280
That what's most important 
is the intrinsic essence, perhaps.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.450
That might be true... but...

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.780
I'm starving.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.460
I wonder what we're having for lunch. 
I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:03.070
Sakura-chan and Masaki's mom cook food
as tasty as pitching a shutout game.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.900
Once we're done eating, let's head 
right back out and surf some more! Okay?

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.420
Welcome home, Big Brother!

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:16.110
Kosuke-san, Yuta-san, 
Naoya-san, good work out there!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.530
Sakura-chan!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.230
We're back.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.240
You have a guest!

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.860
I do?

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.380
Who?

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.800
Another serving, if I may.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.500
Fuke-san?

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:37.730
Of course. You can have 
as many servings as you want.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.110
Thank you. In that case, I will.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.210
Why are you at my house?

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.010
I just happened to be in the area.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.650
You what?

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.230
Here you are, Fuke-kun. Enjoy.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.760
Thank you very much.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.520
Come on, Masaki, 
and the rest of you. Come eat.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.520
Oh, uh... Right.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.750
Thank you for the meal!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.680
I can feel this shirasu-don seeping 
into every fiber of my being.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.040
And this dried sweet potato over rice 
is seriously amazing!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.860
Really?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.460
Um, Fuke-san.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.380
When you say you happened to be passing by...

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.720
Why did you come to Ibaraki at all?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.430
For training. I'm going to 
every seaside around the country.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:25.320
What?

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:31.520
There is an infinite variety of waves.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.060
They never show you the same face twice.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.190
I will ride any wave, no matter 
where, no matter what kind.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.190
That is what this training is for.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.140
I see.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:46.200
So that you can counter any 
conditions you might find... right?

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:47.980
Just what I'd expect from you.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.450
Though that isn't the only 
reason I came to Oarai.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.460
Um, Fuke-san?

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.210
Thank you. It was delicious.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:06.220
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.210
I'll be going on ahead.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.220
Huh?

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.220
The waves are calling me, you see.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.870
Oh dear...

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.220
Thanks for the food! I'm off!

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.170
Thank you for the meal! We're off!

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.750
Come back safe!

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.680
They're all such children, aren't they?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:50.610
<i>We all... just kept riding the waves.</i>

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.280
<i>Again and again...</i>

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.030
<i>None of us made a move 
to get out of the ocean.</i>

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.650
<i>Pushed to the very 
limits of our endurance...</i>

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:14.240
<i>Until we were completely 
exhausted... we just kept riding!</i>

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.250
I feel alive again!

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:34.530
Where are you going after this?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.390
I will head north.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:40.040
First, Soma. Then, Sendai Shinko.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.260
After that, Ishinomaki.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:46.440
In season three, after Sally 
lost faith in her powers,

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.950
she wandered that same course!

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.050
Are you on a pilgrimage 
to all the important sites?

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.300
What are you talking about?

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:59.320
I'm going to train myself 
just as hard as you are!

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:02.560
I'll train both my body 
and mind to their utmost limits!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.060
Fuke-san! Are you going to ride the waves 
from here all the way to Soma?

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:10.510
No. Use your common sense.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.110
Right...

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.830
Bill will be coming for me.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.180
Right.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.710
You'll all be entering too, won't you?

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.660
Huh?

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:31.460
Making certain of that was one 
of the reasons I came here.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.470
The world tournament in four years.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.320
There's a competition to determine 
which athletes will join the team.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:40.720
You'll be entering, won't you?

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.780
A world tournament...

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.240
The members will be selected through...

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.490
...a competition.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.910
Let's all aim for it!

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.900
For the world!

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.650
O-Of course I'm doing it!

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.410
I will go to the world stage!

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.820
To the world!

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:19.680
I think of all of you as my rivals.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:23.930
I will not be beaten.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.400
N-Neither will I!

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:27.930
I won't lose!

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.190
And me! I won't lose!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.670
I won't be beaten!

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.440
I won't lose, either!

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:38.580
Yeah.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.740
Yeah.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.210
Bill?

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:56.150
I came to pick up Rindo-kun, and here
I find you doing something that looks like fun.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.970
And, of course, I won't be beaten, either.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.970
Yeah! And this is for Tanaka!

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.290
Let's go!

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.970
Beyond the waves! To the world!

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.490
Yeah!

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:10.280
Just like Miruru!

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.480
<i>With the new semester just ahead of us,</i>

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:21.980
<i>Kosuke-san, Yuta, and Naoya headed back 
to Shonan and Oita a little before I did.</i>

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.990
<b>Oarai Minami Middle School</b>

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.250
It was only a year ago 
that I was going to school here,

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.840
but it feels like it was forever ago.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.970
Hey!

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:46.890
Is that you, Hinaoka?

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.140
Mr. Nogami!

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.150
You're working pretty hard.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.140
Huh?

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.650
Whenever you or Tanaka 
are in a tournament, I always watch.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.290
I'm looking forward to 
seeing what you can do.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.650
Sir... Thank you!

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:05.660
"The show must go on." Right?

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:08.410
Yes, sir!

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.410
Hey! Tanaka!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:27.440
Hey, Sho! Let's ride some waves!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:27.440
Hey, Sho! Let's ride some waves!

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.610
The show must go on!

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.340
Stop that!

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:43.240
"The show must go on" 
is a nice phrase, isn't it?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.600
Manager! Shoko-san! Hello!

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.470
Welcome, Masaki-kun!

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:09.470
We've got it ready.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:11.470
Thank you.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:19.010
It's just as it was back then.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:19.890
Yeah.

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:22.560
Are you okay now?

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:26.100
Yeah.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.620
Sadness is like a wave.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.200
It surges in and recedes, 
over and over again.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:41.660
But... now you can overcome those waves.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.910
Manager!

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:52.890
Yeah!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.390
The wind's nice again today.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:05.540
<i>On the last day of spring break,</i>

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:09.660
<i>there was a place I wanted to drop 
by before returning to Shonan.</i>

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.660
Let's see... Is it this way?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.670
So this is where Sho grew up, huh?

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.680
<i>Sho...</i>

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:27.350
Let's go surfing!

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.050
Huh?

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:34.060
<i>...met Hayamichi-san here 
in this town and started surfing.</i>

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:37.430
<i>I met Sho...</i>

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.060
Masaki, you sure you just want to watch?

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.310
You should come do it with us.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.320
<i>...and, just like that, I started surfing.</i>

00:14:57.110 --> 00:15:00.740
<i>That day changed my fate, too.</i>

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:19.350
I'm really glad I met you, Sho.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:23.100
Since then, I've wanted to be just like you.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.110
But now I know that isn't right.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.850
I'm going to surpass you, Sho!

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.110
I'm not waiting anymore!

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:35.870
Sho! I'm going on ahead!

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.350
I'm going ahead, you hear?

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.380
Okay, let's go!

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.500
<i>The ocean will tell me.</i>

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.130
<i>They say surfing is like life itself.</i>

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:53.750
<i>If some days the waves are gentle,</i>

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.140
<i>there are some days 
when they're terrifyingly rough.</i>

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.480
<i>We ride those waves, and even 
if sometimes we get pulled under,</i>

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.440
<i>even then, we pull ourselves up.</i>

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.150
<i>We pull ourselves up and stand 
as many times as it takes.</i>

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:09.150
<i>So come on, waves! You big waves!</i>

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:15.660
<i>No matter how huge 
the waves are, I will... We will...</i>

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:18.080
<i>overcome them!</i>

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:55.410
<i>Heading into the world competition, someone 
will be chosen to add their strength to the team!</i>

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.360
<i>Who will it be?</i>

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:04.710
<i>Burning hotter and more 
blindingly than the sun...</i>

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:08.710
Go and shine even brighter!

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.140
Yay! Yeah, yeah!

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:12.340
Big Brother!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.720
Masaki! Hang in there!

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:21.790
<i>Great!</i>

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:23.480
<i>He's grabbed the slimmest of chances!</i>

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:27.010
<i>What concentration.</i>

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:30.610
<i>Miyazaki's bucking bronco. 
Such magnificent dynamism!</i>

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.610
Will you be able to keep up with me?

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:41.300
<i>The Wizard of the Waifu Board.</i>

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:45.220
<i>A quick pan and he nails 
his Perforation Attack!</i>

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:49.590
<i>I don't understand the name 
he created for this move,</i>

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:53.170
<i>but it is truly excellent!</i>

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:56.910
<i>Miruru... Just keep watching me.</i>

00:17:56.910 --> 00:18:01.010
<i>And no matter how your form may change,</i>

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.920
<i>I will keep watching you, too!</i>

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:06.520
M. I. R. U. R. U.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.220
Hollywood Dream!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.280
<i>A freewheeling, science-type guy...</i>

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:21.910
<i>Is his riding based on 
instinct, or calculation?</i>

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.800
<i>Aloha oe!</i>

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:28.860
Aloha!

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:31.520
Surfing is very fun, right?

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.630
<i>He's been riding a board 
for as long as he can remember...</i>

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.490
<i>A born surfer!</i>

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:41.370
<i>With those discerning eyes, 
what does he see beyond the waves?</i>

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.190
<i>Justice!</i>

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:50.400
Progress on the path to the world... 
is just as I calculated.

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:53.200
<i>His playboy era has ended.</i>

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.840
<i>In his new era, he's a man's man.</i>

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:58.970
<i>Plunging straight forward 
with simple honesty...</i>

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:02.020
<i>His hot blood is burning.</i>

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:03.210
<i>For victory!</i>

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.000
Here I go.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.420
<i>He said this...</i>

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.500
<i>"I'm not short on cash!"</i>

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.930
<i>"But no matter how much money I save up, 
there are things I can't buy!"</i>

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:20.310
<i>"Waves and the feeling 
of being one with them!"</i>

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:25.380
<i>Right now, he is one with the waves!</i>

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:34.610
Okay. Now, it's my turn!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:37.410
<b>Masaki
Fight</b>

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:38.360
<b>Go for it!!
Japan</b>

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:38.370
You can do it, Big Brother!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:40.370
You got this! Go!

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.860
<b>Go for it!!
Japan, Represent</b>

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:46.620
Go, go! Let's go!

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.680
You can do it! Go!

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:51.300
Do it! Hang in there!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.500
I love you both!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.080
Hey! Seriously?

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.520
Corgi!

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:56.680
Wow!

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:57.910
A rainbow!

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.980
Hey... There're two!

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:02.690
Oh, it's a double rainbow.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.580
This view is incredible.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.340
It really is.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.950
No rain, no rainbow.

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:14.280
It's a saying here in Hawaii.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:17.190
If it doesn't rain, 
there will never be rainbows.

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:20.020
After difficult things, sad things,

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:22.910
happiness is waiting. 
That's what the saying means.

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:35.880
<i>Masaki, remember what I said?</i>

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.890
<i>The ocean is all connected!</i>

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.120
Watch me, Sho!

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:55.250
<i>Take off!</i>

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:02.710
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:09.680
<i>Let's go surfing!</i>

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:53.990
<b><i>Let's go surfing!</i></b>
